# Reading a SHT temperature & humidity sensor
How to read and visualize a [SHT sensor](https://www.seeedstudio.com/Grove-Temp-Humi-Sensor-SHT41-p-5383.html) with CircuitPython.

## Dependencies

You will need to download and to install following libraries:
- **adafruit_bus_device/**
- **adafruit_sht4x.mpy**

You can find it as part of the [Adafruit CircuitPython Library Bundle](https://circuitpython.org/libraries). Download manually the latest release, but check first that it matches with your CircuitPython version. 

The libraries in each release are compiled for all recent major versions of CircuitPython. Please download the one that matches the major version of your CircuitPython. For example, if you are running 6.0.0 you should download the 6.x bundle.

## Running the example
* Set up the [hardware](#Hardware), connect it to your computer via USB.
* Copy the content of [sht.py](sht.py) to _code.py_ on the _CIRCUITPY_ drive.
* Copy the dependencies into the folder `lib` on the _CIRCUITPY_ drive.
* Consider opening the [serial plotter](https://codewith.mu/en/tutorials/1.2/plotter) (available if you are using the [Mu Python editor](https://github.com/fhnw-imvs/fhnw-idb/wiki/Mu-Python-editor)).
